diagnosis_text:
r8 is an OSPF ABR connected to the backbone (Area 0) exclusively through a virtual link that transits Area 1 (the "invisible bridge" the ticket references). The virtual link itself is operationally healthy — both r4 and r8 show the VLINK0 adjacency as Full. The fault lies in r8's backbone LSDB: r8's Area 0 database contains 72 LSAs while r4's Area 0 database contains 73. The single missing entry is the ASBR-summary (type 4) LSA for the EIGRP ASBR r11 (router-ID 112.1.1.1), which r1 originates in Area 0 with metric 10. 
